{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-torus-hopf-stability","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:torus-hopf-stability","kind":"proposition","title":"Torus knot composites on Bring's surface are stable hadrons","tags":["stability","torus-knot","hadron","euler-characteristic","crossing-energy"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Archimedean.torus_hopf_stability","text":"torus-hopf-stability.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/torus-hopf-stability.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:torus-hopf-stability\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be the Descartes universe with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\chi(A) = -6</code>. Every baryon formed from torus knot generators <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{G}</code> linked by the Hopf link <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{L}_H</code> satisfies the stability condition</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathfrak{E}_{\\mathrm{cross}}(\\mathfrak{H}) &#x3C; 0</code></pre>\n<p>and is therefore a hadron.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/torus-hopf-stability.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"15.5.3"}
